{
  "$comment": [
    "Corpus for `appearance_sanitize_gate_tier3_equivalence` — v4",
    "`lib/image-gen/appearance-resolution.ts` `sanitizeAppearancesIfNeeded`, the",
    "five-rule gate. Until [cc65d6bfc / bug 133] NO harness family and no oracle",
    "case drove that function directly: the story and image-generation tier-3",
    "families reach it only incidentally, and the image one keeps the Concierge OFF",
    "throughout. This family drives it head-on.",
    "",
    "The grid (v4 `406dbdd5a` re-ruled bug 133; P4.D326 RE-SHAPED it) is the",
    "policy {off duty, Moderated with the pre-screen on, Unmoderated} x",
    "imageTargetUncensored {t,f} x classification {safe, dangerous} = 12 rows, each",
    "row's policy resolved from its stored `concierge` settings WITH its `chat`;",
    "plus a customClassificationPrompt row, two sanitizer-answer edges, #76's three",
    "pass-through policies (Moderated without the pre-screen, Locked, an exempt help",
    "chat) each with the target false AND true (AGCASE41..43). Before `406dbdd5a`",
    "the function took isDangerousChat + routesDangerousToUncensored; v4 replaced the",
    "pair with ONE boolean — \"the profile that will actually paint this is",
    "uncensored\" (`isUncensoredImageProfile`). The re-cut kept each old row whose",
    "isDangerousChat was false (its routes flag became the target) and DROPPED the",
    "eight \"flagged\" twins: under the one boolean they collapse onto the kept rows",
    "with identical text, and a twin would share the process-global classification",
    "cache. Tokens are unchanged, so AGCASE05..08 / 13..16 / 21..24 are absent by",
    "design. Rule 1 (target uncensored) answers with its own DEBUG and NO",
    "classifier call in every chat state; rule 2 (no pre-screen) now covers an",
    "Unmoderated chat too (the `&& !routeDirect` arm is gone); the old step 4 is",
    "deleted.",
    "",
    "[4fbdad186] P4.D326 — what a character CARRIES (the Inventory's image phrase,",
    "`carryingDescription`) and the classify text's byte change. A case may override",
    "`clothing` and set `carrying` per character. AGCASE44..52: an EMPTY clothing",
    "classifies the physical description ALONE (`[phys, cloth, carry].filter(Boolean)",
    ".join(' ')` — no trailing space; it was `${phys} ${cloth}`), dangerous and safe;",
    "a carried phrase joins the classify text, the sanitize text becomes `phys. cloth.",
    "carrying` and a CHANGED text clears `carryingDescription` (absent in the",
    "projection); a safe one keeps it; `carrying` + an empty clothing gives v4's",
    "`phys.. carrying` (base `phys.`, then `. carrying`); rule 1 and rule 2 leave the",
    "phrase as written; an echo keeps it; a whitespace-only phrase is no sentence.",
    "",
    "`predicates` (P4.D326 item 2): ten rows driving the REAL",
    "`isUncensoredImageProfile(profile, resolveConciergeSettings(...))` — the null",
    "arm, compatible, the desk match with the flag false and with the key absent,",
    "no desk, an empty-string desk (`Boolean('')`), another desk, Locked (whose",
    "desk is empty), and a string \"true\" (v4 reads `=== true`).",
    "",
    "Each case carries its own TOKEN inside the appearance text. That is not",
    "decoration: the classification cache is keyed by a sha256 of the content and is",
    "process-global on BOTH sides, so two rows sharing appearance text would make the",
    "second one's completion-call comparand measure the cache instead of the gate.",
    "",
    "Comparands per row: the returned appearances (physicalDescription /",
    "clothingDescription / wasSanitized) AND the number of completion calls with",
    "their recorded keys — which is what proves WHICH rule fired. Rules 1 and 2",
    "make zero calls, rule 3-safe makes one, rule 4 (sanitize) makes two.",
    "",
    "NOT compared: `llm_logs`. v4's classify path logs a DANGER_CLASSIFICATION row,",
    "but jest.setup no-ops the logging service and un-mocking it would need this",
    "family to provision a whole instance for a projection two other families",
    "(danger_gatekeeper_tier3, story_background_job_tier3) already diff. Recorded",
    "here so the omission is a decision and not an oversight.",
    "",
    "[97b25fc53] P4.D239 — the drape. Rows AGCASE31..40 pose the sanitize MODE",
    "(`mode`, the 8th argument; absent = v4's `redress` default) and the conceal",
    "reply's `undressed` flag (`undressed`, spliced per character into the answer",
    "whatever the mode). They pin: the three-way merge (changed + undressed; an",
    "unchanged ECHO + undressed keeps its clothing with `wasSanitized` false; changed",
    "+ not undressed); v4's STRICT `=== true` (`\"true\"` and `1` read false); the",
    "junk fallback carrying no `undressed` in conceal; redress dropping a stray",
    "`true`; rule 1 skipping every call in conceal too; a text ending in `.`",
    "(the story builder's `..` is pinned in the story family — here the text rides",
    "through unchanged); and `sanitizeThrows` — v4's `Sanitization failed` WARN arm",
    "in BOTH modes (the N3 gap the Rust header recorded). Comparands gained:",
    "`needsConcealment` (present only when true), `concealPromptCalls` (the mock's",
    "second probe — which prompt the mode picked), and `logLines` (v4's REAL logger",
    "calls for the gate + the sanitizer's pre-call DEBUG, keys in v4's order)."
  ],
